[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4928129298","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120793#issuecomment-4928129298","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120793","id":4928129298,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJb1JEg","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-09T18:06:55Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T18:29:18Z","body":"@HolonProduction Based on the partial review, I've tracked pretty much every vector I've marked as tight that isn't resized often.\r\n\r\nOnly exceptions were `GDScript::(old_)static_variables` (because of the hot reloading concerns) and `GDScriptFunction::CallState::stack` (which is actively resized in the VM).\r\n\r\nIn any case, I'd like to ask if this is good, and if any of them should be tight or not. If `LocalVector::reserve_exact` ever comes to exist, there would be fewer cases to replace.\r\n\r\n**EDIT**: And `GDScriptLambda(Self)Callable::captures`. Not sure if they're created only once, but every creation implies a resize, so better skip the growth c